\newlabel{fig:c01-rooting}{{1.1.3}{4}{One tree, two roots. Rooting at $B$ makes $A$ a child of $B$ and $D$ a child of $B$; rooting at $A$ makes $B$ a child of $A$. The edges do not change, only our view of parent and child does}{figure.caption.10}{}}
